{{!-- My story, told as a VERTICAL stacked timeline — /about's own
variant of partials/journey.hbs (the homepage keeps the horizontal
scroll-snap strip; this page reads top to bottom instead, which
suits a page people are already sitting still to read). Same
chapters, same rail-behind-node technique as .home-path-track /
.activity-rail elsewhere in the theme, just running down the page
instead of sideways — no new JS, .stack-timeline is pure CSS.

⚠ THE YEARS BELOW ARE PLACEHOLDERS — see journey.hbs. Correct both
files together if you fix the real dates. --}}
<section class="section outer">
    <div class="inner">
        <div class="section-head" data-animate>
            <div>
                <span class="kicker">{{> "icons/map-icon"}} {{t "The journey"}}</span>
                <h2>{{t "From job seeker to Salesforce engineer"}}</h2>
                <p>{{t "The road so far — every stop taught something you'll find on this site."}}</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <ol class="stack-timeline" data-animate-stagger>
            <li class="stack-stop">
                <span class="stack-node" aria-hidden="true">{{> "icons/search"}}</span>
                <div class="stack-stop-body">
                    <span class="stack-tag">{{t "The start"}} · <time>2018</time></span>
                    <h3>{{t "Job seeker"}}</h3>
                    <p>{{t "Degree in hand, inbox full of applications. The only real asset: the will to learn anything."}}</p>
                </div>
            </li>

            <li class="stack-stop">
                <span class="stack-node" aria-hidden="true">{{> "icons/zap"}}</span>
                <div class="stack-stop-body">
                    <span class="stack-tag">{{t "First break"}} · <time>2019</time></span>
                    <h3>Accenture</h3>
                    <p>{{t "The offer that started everything — first project, first production incident, first win."}}</p>
                </div>
            </li>

            <li class="stack-stop">
                <span class="stack-node" aria-hidden="true">{{> "icons/fire"}}</span>
                <div class="stack-stop-body">
                    <span class="stack-tag">{{t "The spark"}} · <time>2020</time></span>
                    <h3>{{t "Trailblazer"}}</h3>
                    <p>{{t "Met Salesforce on a project and never left — Trailhead badges by night, real orgs by day."}}</p>
                </div>
            </li>

            <li class="stack-stop">
                <span class="stack-node" aria-hidden="true">{{> "icons/layers"}}</span>
                <div class="stack-stop-body">
                    <span class="stack-tag">{{t "Scale"}} · <time>2022</time></span>
                    <h3>Cognizant</h3>
                    <p>{{t "Bigger enterprises, bigger orgs — the years that taught how real projects actually run."}}</p>
                </div>
            </li>

            <li class="stack-stop">
                <span class="stack-node" aria-hidden="true">{{> "icons/signal"}}</span>
                <div class="stack-stop-body">
                    <span class="stack-tag">{{t "GTM era"}} · <time>2024</time></span>
                    <h3>Twilio</h3>
                    <p>{{t "GTM engineering — where Salesforce meets revenue, data and messaging at speed."}}</p>
                </div>
            </li>

            <li class="stack-stop is-now">
                <span class="stack-node" aria-hidden="true">{{> "icons/cloud"}}</span>
                <div class="stack-stop-body">
                    <span class="stack-tag"><i class="story-now-ping" aria-hidden="true"></i> {{t "Now"}} · <time>2026</time></span>
                    <h3>Education First</h3>
                    <p>{{t "Salesforce Engineer at a global education company — and sharing every lesson here."}}</p>
                </div>
            </li>

            <li class="stack-stop is-next">
                <span class="stack-node" aria-hidden="true">{{> "icons/avatar"}}</span>
                <div class="stack-stop-body">
                    <span class="stack-tag">{{t "Your turn"}}</span>
                    <h3>{{t "You?"}}</h3>
                    <p>{{t "Start your own Salesforce chapter — the courses are free and the path is mapped."}}</p>
                    <a class="btn btn-sm" href="{{@site.url}}/courses/">{{t "Start here"}} {{> "icons/arrow-right"}}</a>
                </div>
            </li>
        </ol>
    </div>
</section>
